Tim Ross wrote:
> 
> I have inherited an AlphaStation 200 4/166 on my desktop, it appears to
> have an ATI video card and 32MB in 4 8 meg simms, the system on powerup has
> no video and makes 3 loud beeps waits about 3 secs makes 3 more beeps then
> nothing... Anyone have any idea what this error is?
> 
> tross@atitech.ca

I believe these codes are correct:

Diagnostic LED Codes

     LED Code      Meaning

        FA         memory test 1 failed
        F9         memory test 2 failed
        F8         memory test 3 failed
        F7         memory test 4 failed
        F2         DROM and flashROM corrupted
        DE         memory test failed
        DD         flashROM ID test failed
        DC         NVRAM test failed
        DB         SCSI test failed
        DA         PCI/ISA bridge test failed
        D9         TOY test failed
        D8         keyboard controller test failed
        D7         Super I/O chip test failed
                   (floppy, parallel port, COM ports)
        D6         interrupt test failed
        D0         power-on selftest passed, DROM console running
        E2         floppy load failed
        E1         flashROM load failed
        20         machine check occurred

Diagnostic Beep Codes

     Beep Code     Meaning

     1-1-4         The SROM code could not read the DROM code or
                   flashROM headers, or
                   there was a checksum failure

     1-2-1         The DROM code detected a TOY failure, or
                   the TOY interrupt did not occur

     1-2-4         The SROM code detected a hard failure (e.g., a
                   Bcache failure)

     1-3-3         The SROM code code not find at least two MBytes
                   of good memory

     3-2-1         The DROM code was unable to read the flashROM
                   so it tried to boot the floppy disk, but this
                   attempt failed because there was either no diskette
                   installed, or the floppy did not have an Alpha
boot                                     block.

     3-2-3         The DROM code tried to boot the floppy (as directed
                   by Jumper J5), but there was no diskette installed.

     3-2-4         The DROM code detected a keyboard/mouse controller
                   failure.

     3-3-1         The DROM code detected a hard failure.  See the LEDs 
                   for more diagnostic information.
                                                                 



