The Fall 1996 OVMS/L&T SIG tapes have gone out to the top of the trees
and to a few sites. You can find the materials at ftp.montagar.com
(Thanks to Dave Cathey) and at ftp.acornsw.com (Thanks to Dick Munroe)
and the DECUS library CD #20 master has been cut.

(Shameless plug: I put a one-disk version of Safety on there. It gives
a reliable undelete (changes "delete" to mean "move to wastebasket" at
file system level), space management, file passwords, anti-Trojan horse
measures, file hiding, softlinks, access controls which can prevent access
with too many privs held, or based on time, location, image, name, etc.,
and a lot of other weird stuff. The Postscript manuals (and text versions)
are in the saveset. You can have an undelete that is RELIABLE (because the files
are captured before deletion), can protect against unauthorized access, have
file passwords, hide files from the unauthorized, do softlinking, monitor
space and prevent it from running out, actively prevent virii and/or Trojan
