Doctor Who wrote:
> 
> I just found a vaxstation 2000. It needs a drive (with OS), and a power

Well, as for the drive, any MFM drive should work if you can actually
get some obscure parameters for it.  Digital designated specific some
MFM drives with its designations and maybe did a few hardware mods just
to make them detectibly different.  Those are more directly supported.

> supply. I figure it would probably be easier to convert a PC power
> supply than to track down a replacement. Does anyone know the pinouts
> for the power supply, and what kind of power it sucks down?

I don't know the specs for the power supply.  Nothing is written on the
power supply itself.  However, it should be in the technical manual
(long out of print).  If somebody has one of those they could look it
up.  All I could do would be to open up the box and measure voltages
with my DMM.  If you want that, tell me.  

> I am also looking at what OS to put on it. I am not going to buy one.
