Jeff, 

From Glen Kelley's response, your Starion uses the LPX motherboard /
riser card format.  This is not at all standard among vendors, which
is a darn shame.  I don't think a kit to install a standard baby-AT
would quite cut it.  There are a lot of physical differences to
overcome here.  And finding a 3rd party LPX board and riser card that
would just happen to fit is a real needle-in-a-haystack, in my
opinion.

I would advise Starion owners (and Venturis and Celebris owners with
LPX format, too) to either stick with what they've got or get new
motherboard, case, and graphics card... Ben Myers


