:Ok then, what does a "KA630-A.V1.3" mean?  A KA630 is not on your list.

   The KA630 is the processor module used in the MicroVAX II and
   VAXstation II series systems.  The list you are responding to
   included most recent non-Q-bus workstations and servers -- the
   MicroVAX 3100, the VAXstation 4000 workstations, and the VAX
   4000-1xx series systems.  The -A suffix was the `timeshare' vs
   `workstation or server' identifier, and the V1.3 is the version
   of the on-board console program.

   Here are most of the Q-bus VAX CPU codes, the VAX-11 codes, the
   VAX 8000-series codes, the VAX 6000-series codes, and the VAX
   7000-series codes, with some specific example applications --
   these CPU modules were used in various other systems, this is
   by no means a complete list of systems with these CPUs, nor
   is this a complete list of all VAX CPU modules...

