  I have used the BA23/BA123 cabinet kits from a KA630 on a KA650/655 with no
problems (I have 3 systems running this way right now). I don't know of any
reason to think that the S-box version would be any different.

> It would seem I need to either get a KA640, or a BA213 cabinet kit for the
> KA650 I have.  What I do not know, is which is the better way to go.  My
> questions to the group are:
>
> 1) Does a KA640 really have on-board Ethernet, or am I missing something?

  Yes, and DSSI.

> 2) How do a KA640 and KA650 compare in performance?

  Funny, I don't remember. By todays's standards, both are pretty abysmal 8-)
If your application involves DSSI disks or Ethernet, the KA640 is probably a
better bet, since those are integrated onto the processor card. I don't re-
member if the KA640 Ethernet is LANCE or SGEC - if it's SGEC it's *lots*
faster than LANCE.

> 3) Am I missing any issues?

  Do you have memory for this box? The boards are compatible between KA640/
650/655 except that not all 640/650 boards work in the 655, but all 655
boards should work in 640/650. MicroVAX II (KA630) memory is *not* compatible.

