Greetings, I hope someone can help...

We are running PSE110 on a small cluster of AlphaStation 250 4/266
workstations running Digital Unix V4.0 (Rev. 386).  (Is that 4.0?
4.0a?)  The default psefarm partition is working fine on 5 of the 6
workstations in the farm.  (At least, lspart shows the members
correctly.)  But on one of the hosts, trying to run lspart results in
the following errors:

9664:/usr/bin/lspart: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/bin/lspart: pse_farm_port
9664:/usr/bin/lspart: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/bin/lspart: have_txt_records
9664:/usr/bin/lspart: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/bin/lspart: gather_loadinfo
9664:/usr/bin/lspart: /sbin/loader: Fatal Error: this executable has unresolvable symbols

Similarly, '/usr/sbin/farmd farmd -farm psefarm' yields:

9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/sbin/farmd: which_db_entry
9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/sbin/farmd: create_new_member
9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/sbin/farmd: reorder_database
