9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/sbin/farmd: pse_farm_port
9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/sbin/farmd: wsf_downcase
9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Error: unresolvable symbol in /usr/sbin/farmd: have_txt_records
9222:/usr/sbin/farmd: /sbin/loader: Fatal Error: this executable has unresolvable symbols

As you might imagine, inetd spends most of its time executing this
repeatedly!  (Lots of pacct files...)

I was a bit suspicious of the PSE110 installation on this host.  It
still had /usr/opt/PSE100 in place and /sbin/init.d/farmd still
pointed to the PSE100 version.  But as far as I can tell, the binaries
/usr/sbin/farmd and /usr/bin/lspart (for example) point to the correct
PSE110 versions.

It seems that this host is missing some shared library?  Or some other
component?  "setld -i" reports that all of the requirements listed in
Table 1-1 on page 1-5 of the HPF and PSE Installation Guide (PostScript
version) are "installed."  (But that doesn't mean "installed correctly,"
does it?)

Any suggestions would be appreciated.  I need this to work ASAP.
Thanks for your help.

