In article <5efhpb$40g$1@news.fas.harvard.edu>, GB <berriz@husc.harvard.edu> writes:
:...To get a quote for this
:software, we must put together a portfolio of what we want.  The
:problem is that no one in our lab has any experience at all with DEC
:software.  In particular, we don't know what specific software items
:are essential or desirable for the kind of work we do here....

  The Software Product Description (SPD) is key to your task: the SPD
  contains an overview, and detailed information on what each product
  supports.  SPDs are available at Digital's web site.  That list you
  posted has the relevent SPD numbers for each of the packages.

  You might want FUSE, DCE, Fortran, the C development extensions stuff,
  the development toolkit, the Athena stuff, and C++.  You might also be
  interested in the TruCluster software, PHIGS, GKS, shadowing, and a few
  of the other packages.

  Many of the packages in the listing you posted will likely be rather
  uninteresting to you, but only you know your local applications and
  local requirements...

