You could make an entry at the boot section of the console:

LOADIDENTIFIER	Installation per CD
SYSTEMPARTITION	scsi(0)cdrom(<ID of CD-Roms>)fdisk(0)
OSLOADER	<Your path to linload>linload.exe
OSLOADPARTITION	scsi(0)cdrom(<ID of CD-Roms>)fdisk(0)
OSLOADFILENAME	\milo\<systemname>\milo
OSLOADOPTIONS	boot -t iso9660 sr0:/kernels/<systemname.gz>
                bootfile=/kernels/<systemname.gz> root=/dev/scd0
                load_ramdisk=1

Maybe you must restart your sytem a second time if your kernel
isn't found.


