>Yes you should and you should build them as Advanced File System.  AdvFS
>means you never have to fsck again.  It's built proof.   I can pull the
>plug on one a my Alpha's anytime.
>Jack Patteeuw

Read: Even if you might want to fsck, you can't !

I once had a screwed AdvFS on my Alpha due to a SCSI bus hang (bus terminator
accidentally unplugged), and the file system was so damaged that the
kernel paniced upon any attempt to touch the file system.  No chance
to save anything, we had to restore from tape.  Fortunately, we had a
backup that was only one day old :-)

Lesson learned: AdvFS is fine (I still use it), but it's not bulletproof.
Nothing can replace a backup.  

