R.H.Ettrich wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> if you run the Xerver with 16bpp colordepth under LinuX, the programm
> mpeg_play is claiming to require 8bpp.
> With 32bpp it is working with the option "-dither color", but not
> with 16.
> Has anybody already solved the problem or is there another mpegplayer
> for LinuX which can handle the problem?

Try 'xdpyinfo' in your console window and look at the 'color depth'
value in the visual list. If this is 15, then the original mpeg_play
won't work. Two ways to solve the problem:

1. Try configure your X-Server to use a 'color depth' of 16 instead
   of 15 (in Xsetup for AccelX choose '65536 colors' instead of
   '32768 colors').

2. Use my FixPix patches for mpeg_play at
   http://www.esc.de/homes/guivol/fixpix/
   Thus mpeg_play will work with 15 bit color depth!

Regards,
Guido



