When it boots it will indicate the CPU type as KAxx. Below is a list which
I believe to be largely correct (at least it has been right for all the ones
I've ever had the opportunity to check):

	KA41-A for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 10/20
	KA41-B for the VAXserver 3100 Model 10/20
	KA41-C for the (original?) InfoServer (???)
	KA41-D for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 10e/20e
	KA41-E for the VAXserver 3100 Model 10e/20e
	KA42-A for the VAXstation 3100 Model 30/40
	KA42-B for the VAXstation 3100 Model 38/48
	KA43-A for the VAXstation 3100 Model 76
	KA45 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 30/40 (different size enclosures)
	KA46 for the VAXstation 4000 Model 60
	KA47 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 80
	KA48 for the VAXstation 4000 VLC
	KA49-A for the VAXstation 4000 Model 90/90A
	KA49-B for the VAXstation 4000 Model 95
	KA49-C for the VAXstation 4000 Model 96
	KA50 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 90
	KA51 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 95
	KA52 for the VAX 4000 Model 100
	KA53 for the VAX 4000 Model 105
	KA54 for the VAX 4000 Model 106
	KA55 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 85
	KA56 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 96
	KA57 for the VAX 4000 Model 108
	KA58 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 88
	KA59 for the MicroVAX 3100 Model 98

Antonio

