Don Royal wrote:
> 
> Re: DECpcXL Server 486
> Does anyone know what CPU upgrades are available? The CPU socket is a
> three series and the daughtercard is labeled with a barcode TA41000056!
> Are there daughtercards available? If so where and at what price?? Will
> the daughtercard I have accept a regular pentium chip or only an
> overdrive chip?
> I have already downloaded the BIOS upgrades.

Digital sells "Powergrade" upgrades, but these are quite expensive and,
for
the DECpc XL Server, include replacement of the motherboard to bring you
essentially up to a Celebris XL.  More cost-effective is the Pentium
OverDrive
chip, which is what you must use on this daughtercard - a regular
Pentium chip
won't fit (and wouldn't work anyway).  However, if you do decide to go
for the
Powergrade upgrade, you can get a P166 or maybe even a P200 - for a
price.  Call
1-800-DIGITAL to get part numbers and the name of a reseller.
