>> which are not in Windows NT as I understand it.
> 	That's interesting! Did RMS-32 support Prologue 3 from the start?

No, before Prologue 3 there was Prologue 2 for indexed files.

> How was SYSUAF.DAT organized under VMS V1 if indexed files didn't exist?

It was a fixed length record sequential file kept in alphabetic order.

A prominent Field Test site in the V1 days was an academic site (lots
of users) run by a fellow named Doug.  Since the site assigned usernames
by surnames, and Doug's surname was Wilson, DEC got plenty of feedback
about slow logins due to the need to search the entire file to the end.

Larry Kilgallen



