potomactom@aol.com (PotomacTom) wrote:

>I understand that the Starion computers are no longer made by Digital. 
>Any advice/info would be appreciated on how I can upgrade my Starion 915
>computer's modem from 14.4 to 33.6.

>Tom Dercola
>e-mail:  PotomacTom@aol.com


Hey Tom-

As a Starion 910 owner, I've upgraded modems a couple of times. I
currently run a US Robotics Sportster modem along with the original
Telecommander. Check which com port is open on your 'puter, set the
jumpers on the USR modem for that port, plug it in to the open slot,
then use Win95's "detect new hardware" option in the control panel.
Win95 will then detect your new modem for you and install the correct
drivers. Then just make a new connection for your isp usuing the new
modem. USR includes software for faxing with the new modem, so you can
stop using Fax Talk. To make it really slick, use a double jack on
your phone line to connect both modems. Then make sure your isp is
33.6 equipped. The only problem I've encountered is not being able to
use the duplex speaker phone on the Telecommander. But isn't that what
picking up the phone is for anyway? The Sound Blaster part of the
Telecommander card isn't bothered a bit by a new modem.

Rich H.
