PotomacTom wrote:
> 

FIRST:  Is there a Digital answer to upgrading my modem from 14.4 to
33.6, 
while maintaining the minimum features I already have in the
TeleCommander 2500XL?  

Digital does not offer any upgrades to increase the speed of the modem.
The
modem speed is fixed by the hardware chip set used on the modem.

SECOND:  Is there another non-Digital-supported modem which will get me 
upgraded to 33.6 while maintaining the minimum features I already have
in 
my current modem?  

There are a number of modem/sound cards available from Creative Labs
(VoiceBlaster), Boca Research (SE2880), and US Robotics (I can't recall
the name). Each of these products offer the same level of functionality;
ie. 16-bit sound, modem and voice (voicemail and speakerphone). You
would
not be able to use the same applications that are used for the
Telecommander.
Each vendor has their own set of applications that are tailored to their
card.
The question as to whether or not these offer 33.6, you would need to
contact
the vendors (or look in the WEB).

THIRD:  Would I have to physically remove the current modem and install 
the newer modem in its slot, or does the TeleCommander 2500XL stay in
place
and a newer modem installed in another slot?

PCs can support more than one modem, so if you purchased a new 33.6
modem, you 
would not be required to remove the existing Telecommander (you would
have to
set the new modem to different com port and IRQ so as to not conflict
with
the existing Telecommander). Note that this is for the modem only, not
the
voice functions (its not clear to me if a modem that included voice
functions
would function properly in a system that contained a voice modem - it
might work
since the modem is the part the provides the voice functions and not the
sound
card).

While PCs can support more than one modem, they can only support one
sound card.
So you you purchased one of the above mentioned solutions, you would
have to
remove the Telecommander.

