c'est moi wrote:

> I heard about some place that has managed to make
> a 8088 compatible chip running at > 2000MHz. Considering
> that most of the world's software is still 16 bit, my

I think you are referring to the chips being designed
at the little-known "Intel East" factory in Troy, New York.
The chips in this series are named after famous bodies
of water in Upstate NY, including:

Hudson
Onondaga
Saquoit Creek
Love Canal

The Hudson is having some technical difficulties;
programs start out clean and fast-moving, but become
sluggish and polluted as they near completion.
The Onondaga had electrical problems, due to the
high conductivity substrate, which apparently includes
portions of the Gambino Family PMOS (peat moss).  The
most promising is the Love Canal, which unfortunately
requires several kilos of transformer oil to manufacture
one chip.



