G.L.J. Oppers <masc@wish.net> writes:
> Someone gave me 7 boxes and said they are "DECserver 200/DL"'s.
> Hmmm...  great. What is a decserver 200/dl??? what is it used for?

  It's a variant of the DECserver 200 with data leads (hence DL) only (no
modem control).

  It's a terminal server box with 8 serial ports and 1 Ethernet port that
speaks DEC's proprietary LAT protocol. The CPU is some sort of Motorola
68K part. It needs to download its operating software from a DEC host using
the "MOP" protocol.

> Is it worth anything?

  That depends if you have a use for it/them. The usual asking price I've
seen for DS200/MC units (full modem control) is US $50. Of course, that's
the price a vendor wants to sell you one. They may not offer you any money
if you want to sell them one.

  Somebody posted here a week or so ago that they wanted to write some TCP/
IP code for the box. That would make it a bit more useful for many hobbyists.

