Hi,

Geoff Shukin (gps@link.ca) wrote:
: I just purchased a Microvax 2000 from a surplus place.  I hooked up a VT
: to what I thought was the serial port (DB25 with arrows over the
: connector).  The machine chirps and nothing is displayed on the screen. 
: Not even garbage!

: I opened the case and checked the Power Supply.  All looks fine.

: Our local Digital Tech suggested that the 2000's required a special
: connector that goes over the DB 9 and DB15 ports on the back.

The console must be connected to the 9-pin "printer" port. The pinout is
as follows:

2-TxD
3-RxD
7-GND

In addition, you need to make a connection btw. pins 8 and 9 on the VAX side.
This tells the MicroVAX to use the serial console (or was this inly required
for the VAXstation 2000 - not sure ...).

Hope this helps,
regards,
	Michael Engel	(engel@unix-ag.uni-siegen.de)




