Just to be clear, this was a case of having the software around
and thinking 'well, the worst thing that can happen is that
it doesn't work.'  If I didn't have it, I wouldn't have bought
it to install just for this test.  With that in mind, we installed
it and ran a couple short programs.  Frankly, I was suprised it
worked at all, albeit very slowly ( I only ran the program
once, so I assume it was sitting in emulation mode ).
Personally, I wouldn't recommend doing this for running
real work (maybe debugging if I can make it go faster), but
since compilers seem to be a hot topic for people interested
in the Alpha machines, I thought it was worthwhile to post
my experience with this.

If nothing else, it says that DEC came up with a pretty darn
good translator to be able to take an Intel compiler and make
it work on an Alpha.

On another note, does DEC have any plans for a Linux port
of their F90 compiler ?

Jeff



