We're looking at buying an AlphaStation 500/333.  Since we're planning
to use it as a CPU server, we'd like to get the cheapest possible
graphics system.  I really don't care how slow it is, as long as I can
plug in a standard monitor on the rare occasions when I need to use
the console (i.e., when something breaks).

DEC claims that the cheapest supported graphics card is a "PBXGB-AA"
(a PowerStorm 3D30 with 2 MB, according to info from DEC's web site).
This thing lists for $800; with academic discount, we can get it for
an amazing bargain price of $500.

After a week and a half of phone calls, we finally heard from a
technical guy at DEC who said that the PB2GA-JA (PowerStorm 3D10)
graphics card "should work".  But the sales guy wouldn't even give us
a price, since that card is "not supported on the AlphaStation 500".

So... has anyone out there used any cheap PCI graphics card under
Digital Unix?  Are there drivers?  Is this even possible?

[Note to DEC Marketing/Sales, just in case they actually see this: you
would have had our $8000 a week ago if you would just sell us what we
want.]

- Derek



