EV4=21064
EV5=21164
EV6=21264

The 4,5,6 mentioned in alphastations usually refers to the generation
of the cpu.  So a 2100/4/275 is a 275 Mhz 21064.  A 2100/5/300 is a 300 Mhz
21164.   

I actually like the scheme....

Much better then say a HP K200?210?400? 460? 480? 260? D380?

