|>that both of them are bad?  and what are my options at this point considering
|>the fact that I own the machine, monitor, keyboard, mouse, and a small
|>intoductory text?  I heard something to the effect that even If I were to get
|>a new drive, I would need a maintenance tape/disk to format the #$@! thing.
|>

Before writing off your disk or controller, check the cabling. In the BA23 box
(the one without wheels) it is very easy to have the two cables from
the bulkhead to the drive not quite pushed in properly. It happens to me
about 25% of the time (more if I'm in a hurry :-). Push home the connectors
in the bulkhead and at the drive. (Obviously check that the cables are in the
correct connectors while you are at it). If things still do not work, check
that none of the pins in the bulkhead are bent.


