Nearly all alphas are currently Digital computers.  Most 'clone'
makers currently start with a DEC EB164 or PC164 motherboard, and add
their own peripherials.

Have a look at http://www.digital.com:80/SP4161.  This is the
'software product description' for Digital UNIX.  It lists supported
hardware.  Unfortunately, this supported hardware is presented in DEC
lingo.  Eg, you'd never know that a DE500 (PCI Fast Ethernet) was a
21140 based ethernet card & you'd be able to use an SMC or Kingston in
its place.

As a rule of thumb:

scsi controllers: ncr810 or ISP1020
disks:		  any scsi disk should work just fine
CD-ROM:		  DEC RRD4x, or Toshiba (T)XM5301B/D1
graphics bds:     DEC ZLXp-e{1,2,3}, or a S3 Trio 64 PCI card
Network:	  DEC Tulip (21{0,1}40) based PCI cards (like many SMC &
		    Kingstons, or DEC DE435 or DE500
Kbd:		  any pc kbd with ps/2 style connector
Mouse:		  logitech mouseman with ps/2 style connector

<snip>

