George Erhart wrote:

> I have seen a lot of benchmark data (Spec, Byte, etc) that compares
> the Alpha to other CPUs (HP-PA, Sun-SPARC, SGI-MIPS, etc). Most of the
> Alpha benchmarks seem to be from either VMS or Unix based systems.
> Since compiler technology is clearly a contributing factor to performance,
> I would like to know what is the quality of the code produced by the
> "Microsoft Visual C++ V4.0 for RISC platforms" product. I am keenly
> interested in how well it optimizes for floating point computation in
> the vain of streaming multiply/adds.

All of the compilers for standard languages on Alpha platforms provided
by Digital or Microsoft use the GEM compiler back-end for optimization
and code generation.  While there are a few differences in the
information
provided to the back end by the different front ends, the actual
back-end
compiler technology is all shared, so (for example) the same
optimization
technology used for floating point for FORTRAN for Unix is available
in Visual C++ for Windows NT on Alpha.

