Do not forget that many now refuse to go VMS/DIGITAL for new
applications because of its uncertain future and because it is
definitely no longer mainstream.

I made the mistake of pitching a VMS/ALL-IN-1/TEAMLINKs solution which
works today to a group whose leader works for a large US bank and the
solution was refused simply "because Digital has no future". The group's
leader consulted his in-house gurus and came to that conclusion. 

They did not look at the stability of VMS, the quality, robustness or
software
or the fact that I had proved to them during a year long demo that the
solution worked. They just didn't want to commit to a solution that was
not "maintream".
That group's leader did not even try the software. He wanted something
HOT and TRENDY, no realizing that trends change very fast and the
solution which I piched would have solved their needs solidly.

Nop. They just wanted something that was HOT *TODAY*. Not even trying to
compare the expected lifetime of my solution against that of the trendy
solutions that they wanted.

So, when top guys have such opinions of Digital and VMS, like it or not,
corporate decisions are seriously affected by such opinions
notwithstanding any technical merits and preferences by the grunts
working down below.

This is why I feel that right now, most VMS sales depicted by Digtal are
really upgrades of existing sites who are too much momentum built-up to
change to other platforms easily.



