   I happen to have some info on the RZ28-E here, which shows
  the SCSI ID jumpers and termination jumper as below:
 
 
     Looking at the RZ28-E with the electronics module
    facing upwards and the SCSI connector and PWR connector
    towards the rear, the drive-busy LED is at the front
    right-hand corner.
 
     Adjacent to the drive-busy LED, the row of pins
     are:
 
 
             ::::::'::: || <--- BSY LED
 
                    421 <-----SCSI ID
 
         The spinup jumper is also on this strip of pins
        and is located on the fourth pair from the left.
 
 
     The terminator jumpers are adjacent to the SCSI connector
     and are:
 
           SCSI CONNECTOR        PWR CONN
       _______________________________________
 
 
            .  .  Enable
            .  .  Unused
            .  .  Power
 
            termination
             jumpers
 
 
 
       The above is for an RZ28-E.
 
       Hope this helps,
 
