Btw, it's not the chip per se that has the memory interface. Both the
21164A and 21164PC interface to a memory interface, and those can
change.

E.g., the older DEC workstations use the 21172 chipset (which supports
page-mode DRAM, I think), but the newer PWS 433a/500a uses the PYXIS
chipset, which supports SDRAM.

Thus, you could imageine 21164PC based systems with both memory
subsystems.

What I want to know is when will they have one that supports RAMBUS.

