Lowell O. Turner <lotlbbt@radix.net> writes:
> ?4B CTRLERR, DUA0
> ?06 HLT INST
>     PC = 00000EE6
> Failure.
> >>>
>
>    Does this mean that the controller is bad, the disk drive is bad, or
> that both of them are bad?  and what are my options at this point considering
> the fact that I own the machine, monitor, keyboard, mouse, and a small
> intoductory text?  I heard something to the effect that even If I were to get
> a new drive, I would need a maintenance tape/disk to format the #$@! thing.

  A VSII normally has either an RQDX2 or an RQDX3 in it. The RQDX2 is an
M8639 card (it'll be on the metal handle in purple ink, and it should be
the last card in the backplane, a full-width (quad) card). The RQDX3 is
an M7555 card (white ink on a purple plastic handle, half-width (dual)
card).

  As long as your new RQDXn has equal or newer ROMs (and you can re-use the
old ROMs from your old card) you should be able to swap it. An RQDX2 is may-
be $25 to $50 and an RQDX3 is maybe $100 to $200, both from reputable vendors
(I like Compunet, 800-767-9779, ask for Tom and tell him I sent you).

  It's unlikely it clobbered the disk, though you might ask for prices on
disk drives as well.

  You could have a 3rd-party MFM/ESDI/SCSI controller, but that's less likely.
You could open the box and post what boards you have here and someone will
help identify them.

