> Any chance of a Digital person making available the text
> of Digital's presentations (on the 21264 and 21164 DEC/Mitsubishi
> chip) at last week's ISSC Conference?
> 
>         -doug

Two extremely excellent presentations by Digital. Bruce Gieseke talked
about the 21264 at 40 SPECint95/60 SPECfp95 (600 MHz, 8 GB/sec system
memory bandwidth, 9.6 GB/sec read/write bandwidth, 2x improvement in
branch prediction) which taped out last December. Prototypes demoed even
earlier. Fully verified pass one by end of 1CQ97.

Anil Jain talked about the 21164PC. Design center is now 550 MHz (at
which speed it delivers 15 SPECint95/20 SPECfp95), chip has been run as
fast as 625 MHz. It booted WNT on 550 MHz first pass silicon.

Intel presented a 433 MHz MMX P6 processor which apparently is water
cooled. Technology demo only. Evasive on power consumption and
performance, but 15 SPECint95 seems plausible at 433 MHz.

Sun showed off a 330 MHz UltraSPARC II that delivers 13 SPECint95/17.7
SPECfp95. It's in production now and will show up in the Ultra
Enterprise 10000 server.

Further lurid details on ISSCC 97 will be available in my newsletter.

