Anybody out there have any advice/warnings about
buying Alpha clones?  I'm looking at the 500 MHz
21164-based beasts.  Almost everybody has one built
around the PC164 board w/ 1Mb cache, which I under-
stand from past NG posts should bring performance
down compared to the EB164 board that's in Digitals
500 and 600 Alphas.  So, e.g. SPECfp95 should go
from 20 to about 13. Coupla mail-order folks offer 
these, e.g. Enorex, ASL, SWT, for around $6500 if 
you run Linux.

A different deal is offerred by Microway, which
has a *2* Mb cache version for about $2000 more,
again with Linux.

So, anybody have bad experiences with mail order
Alpha clones from these guys?  Anybody find running
Linux a severe disappointment vs. DU?  Anybody think
1 Mb -> 2 Mb cache upgrade will not improve typical
smallish Fortran/C mathematical (e.g. numerical
integration) code by 20 - 30% depending on program
size? 

Thanks for any and all responses in advance.

Christopher Grayce
UCI Department of Chemistry
(remove _ in e-mail address above to respond directly)



