I had an unplanned power outage on my AlphaStation (yeah, Bozo kicked
the power socket) and managed to toast a ufs file system on a partition 
of an RZ28 disk. The disk itself seems fine, no errors in the log, 
reads with dd, scu verify OK etc. but ufs_fsck hangs after:

root@koetsu [~simond] :-] /sbin/ufs_fsck -n /dev/rrz1b
** /dev/rrz1b (NO WRITE)
** Last Mounted on /source
** Phase 1 - Check Blocks and Sizes

