First off ... because of marketing decisions, we are looking to move
from our current UnixWare 1.1.3/Intel Pentium platform to something
in Windows NT domain. (Most of our customer base seems to be following
the pied-piper of redmond down the Windows NT path.) Since NT is offered
(and has a future on) the DEC Alpha platform, we are considering it
as a candidate for using as a compute server. As such, I have ordered
several 500Mhz Alpha systems ...

Anyway.

I have seen a lot of benchmark data (Spec, Byte, etc) that compares
the Alpha to other CPUs (HP-PA, Sun-SPARC, SGI-MIPS, etc). Most of the
Alpha benchmarks seem to be from either VMS or Unix based systems. 
