>* The 21164pc will have better memorybandwidth due to SDRAM

Really?  I'm not sure of that.  Appealing to the lower-end broad-based
demand market, a machine which depends on SDRAM isn't necessarily what
DEC will produce.  SDRAM costs a lot more than EDO or FPM RAM.


>like a noticable difference. Though, from what I've understood the SDRAM
>alphas will _not_ have 2nd or 3rd level cache, which seems like a bad

It depends on your application.  If your application streams through 
an amount of memory >> cache, bandwidth is going to be more important
to you than memory cache.  Also, with fewer layers of cache, your latency
to main memory will improve quite a lot, so you win twice on applications
which aren't cache-friendly.

>* How much is a pc164+cpu+cache (something like 366-433Mhz and 1-2M cache)

Well, a 500MHz pc164 with 2Mcache and 128M RAM and 2G disk cost us about $6.5k.
