> I need to know what the jumpers for an rz57 disk are.

With the drive upside down, the scsi connectors on top pointing towards
you, the drive selector connector is on the right of the scsi connector,
the pins are Left to Right 1,2,3,4....  On the RZ58, the 4th pin is the
spinup pin.  On the RZ56 there isn't one.

RZ55, RZ56 RZ57, and RZ58 Drive SCSI ID

SCSI ID	3	2	1
0	Out	Out	Out
1	Out	Out	In
2	Out	In	Out
3	Out	In	In
4	In	Out	Out
5	In	Out	In
6	In	In	Out
7	In	In	In

You can set the RZ57 and RZ58 to spin up when you apply power to the
host system. Note that when the jumper is removed on the RZ57, the spin
up option is enabled; when the jumper is in place on the RZ58, the spin
up option is enabled.

When the spin up option is disabled, you can spin up the drive using an
SCSI command.

(the jumper is just underneith the power connector...)

