  This is the absolutely most common failure of RD53's (just like bad bear-
ings are the most common fault on the RD54's).

  Someone who spent days on this (not me!) decided that the problem was
excessive current draw by the spindle motor. I don't think they had a long-
term fix, but I think they had some workaround to let the disk spin up long
enough to be backed up.

