large numbers of files), online backup, and improved write performance 
(via write-behind caching) delivered in Spiralog Version 1.0, Spiralog 
Version 2.0 users will be pleased to find:

	- Online volume management; to dynamically grow the 
          storage topography visible to the file system.

	- Clones that are shutdown-persistent, user-visible and 
          readable; for increased storage management flexibility.
 
	- Reduced and predictable resource consumption; memory and 
	  CPU requirements will be on par with those of Files-11 today.

	- Enabled disk quotas.

   ******************************************************************
     Leveraging What We've Learned to Bring the Best to Both Worlds  
   ******************************************************************

From the outset, customers have been enthusiastic about Spiralog's 
online backup features and scalability attributes.  They also value 
the investment protection offered by Spiralog's coexistence with their 
existing file system (Files-11 applications run unchanged on Spiralog).  
However not all environments can easily adapt to a major on-disk-
structure change.

As a result, OpenVMS has modified the file system product rollout to 
more rapidly bring many of the benefits valued by Spiralog customers, 
specifically online backup and write performance -- to the broader 
Files-11 customer base.

Coming in calendar year 1997, Files-11 customers will be provided:

	- A safe, reliable and easily managed means to allow 
	  them to perform online backups with "zero-downtime".

	- A new write-behind cache that provides excellent RMS 
	  indexed file and RU Journaling application performance, 
	  functions better in clustered Alpha environments, and 
          scales more effectively than VIOC.
	  	
In addition, from Files-11 we will provide the ability to use your 
OpenVMS server as the centralized, safe, reliable and ever-available 
environment for your NT data!  Windows NT clients can take advantage of 
physically centralized storage and the high availability provided by 
OpenVMS Clusters.  Plus, online backup will be extended to Windows NT 
clients via served volumes on OpenVMS.  


