 > So why let it depend on the CPU whether this is considered
 > compilable or not ?

The number of people SGI has working on compilers is finite; they may
have decided not to expend the time trying to backport this particular
f90 feature into the f77 compiler, but if you need it, you have it in
the actual f90 compilers.  So use the SGI f90 compilers to compile
your code, specifying -mips3 -n32 so that the resulting executable
will run on any system which can run IRIX 6.2 or higher.

