: |The biggest hurdle is getting over the now-false assumption that you can
: |cast a pointer to an int safely.
: That's never been a true assumption, only a common one.

Agreed.  I also don't think getting over the size issue is all that
hard.  It's mostly a 'lint' issue, and given good lint technology (such
as DEC's 'lint -Q') it's not a big hurdle.  It was harder to find all
the 'sizeof(ip address) == sizeof(int)' assumptions etc.  Another
hard thing is supporting both 32 and 64 bit binaries (something
DEC had the luxury of avoiding).

