>So how much memory did the original Unix boxes have?

Probably less, but I think the original PDP 11 that unix was 
designed on had 64K.

And although the PC originally only came with 64K (or maybe it
was 16k?) DOS 2.0, which introduced some Unix-like ideas, was
designed with the expectation of more RAM. I remember going to
DOS 2.1 on an XT clone with 640K around 1985, and for me that
was a 10x jump (from a 64K TRS80 Model 1).

