Digital should at least try to make something available that typical
individuals can buy (and no, not PC clones--we have hordes of PC clone
manufacturers anyways).  For example, some companies are selling Alpha
based systems that are reasonably priced (about $3k - like a high end
PC).  A relatively simple thing to do would be to have non-commercial
use OpenVMS license that is reasonably priced.  That wouldn't cost them
much (unless too many people start buying it and using it in business). 
