time interval? At our fully redundant network, we badly need such a 
feature for setting hardware addresses in switch address tables, this 
ensures there will be no problems when some switch-enclosure or some 19" 
racks power fails!

I know on Wellfleet and Cisco routers there's a feature called BOFL 
(breath-of life) sending proprietary packets to their own interface, 
enabling the switch to update the address table in case of a switchover 
to another hub.

