The last time I saw a personal IBM mainframe?  How about 5 seconds ago?
The first time?  About 10 years ago.

Seriously, I have a pair of the IBM P/370 (Personal/370) cards in my PS/2s.
These cards implement the full S/370 architecture (16M memory, etc.) on a
card that fits into a PS/2.  I run VM/ESA (-370 Feature) on them.  They're
designed to be single user systems, although they will support multiple
users.

Oh, and yes, they're obselete, having been replaced by the P/390, which
implements the full ESA/390 architecture, allowing use of VM/ESA, MVS/ESA,
etc. on them.

