IMO, the AXPpc 150 was an inexpensive workstation, not a "pc".  
The Alpha XL was also an inexpensive workstation, not a "pc".  
And any "alpha pc" chip or "21164pc" chip or "AlphaPC 164" board 
is not a "pc" unless it *sold* like a pc -- i.e. not thru 
dealers, but thru "pc" channels (mail order catalog, consumer 
retail, or mail order direct).  

I believe that the first brand of workstation (Digital, HP, Sun, 
etc) to be sold mostly thru "pc" channels will increase in market 
share.  The Digital AlphaPC 164 system board is close, it has 
everything but the brand name.




