Ok, I was able to find a few minutes to do some research, and it appears
that the 16KB model was the 5150-1, which had an announced price of
$1,265.  This announcement was dated 820407 (April 7, 1982), and was in
announcement letter number 182-023 (Although I've found a cryptic reference
to a 5150-813, which was apparently also a 16KB model, although I'm missing
the particular announcement letter which announced it (in December 1981?)).

Thus, the floppy based models were the first available, and the non-floppy
models were available later.  All of the early PCs had the cassette
interface.

Dave

