This stuff comes up every about 6 months.  If you were closer than 
Australia I would fax you the manual sheets.

Looking at my shelf I find I have 3 LA50 Printer Refer Manuals
(EK-0LA50-RM-002).  The first 2 people who send me their US 
snail mail address can have them for free.  They still have the 
reader's comments card in them.  If you do not hear back from me,
you were not one of the first 2.

>Can any one post the dip switch lists ? 

SW1, is closer to the platen(big black roller).  SW2 is closer to the 
front.  The maximum Baud rate is 4800.  That is what usually throws 
people off.

Here are the switches(All open except SW2-7 is the default):

SW1-1 to SW1-4 are for nationality.  All open is USA and SW1-1 closed and 
the rest open is Britain.  


SW1-5 graphics aspect ratio

ratio   dots/inch     Switch position

2 to 1    144            open
2.5 to 1  180            closed


SW1-6 Protocol

Open    XON/XOFF
Closed  Ready/Busy


SW1-7  Signal condition

Busy=high   Open
ready=low

Busy=low    Closed
ready=high


SW1-8 Margin

Open = Truncate
closed = wrap


SW2-1 to SW2-3 Baud rate

all open = 4800

SW2-4 to SW2-6 Data format Switches

open    closed closed 7 bits odd parity
closed  closed closed 7 bits even parity
open    open   closed 7 bits plus 8th bit mark
closed  open   closed 7 bits plus 8th bit space
open    closed open   8 bits odd parity
closed  closed open   8 bits even parity
open    open   open   8 bits no parity 


I can find no information in the manual for SW2-7 and 
SW2-8.  On all of my switches are in the Open 
position except SW2-7.  The manual shows my configuration 
as the default. 

>Also on an LA210 one used to be
>able to print out current settings on the printer, can one do that on the
>LA50 and how ?
>
There is no way to print out the settings, but you can do a 
self test by turning the power off, holding down the form feed 
and turning the power on and then releasing the form feed 
button.  To stop the test, turn off the printer.

Mine are connected to a DEC 3000 300, 2100A, and a 
DECSERVER 200a.  I have had no problems with this setup.  
I use them to print out labels.  I use them because you 
can print out a single 3 line label and have it user 
accessable with the print head at the top of then next 
label.

I hope this helps.  good luck!

