Does the device claim to be Optical or Direct Access?  I'd guess
that none of the ULTRIX SCSI drivers will recognize Optical devices.
If the device can be made to pretend to be a Direct Access device
(disk), then the disk driver should work.  For versions using
the SCSI CAM driver, a device entry in /sys/data/cam_data.c may
help a little if the drive needs any special features.

>on my system, it is identified at the console prompt, but isn't identified
>by kernel during boot procedure.

ULTRIX was in the habit of having "device" lines for all possible
SCSI disks and tapes for each adapter.  If you've edited that down
to just what you have, that could be the problem.  I don't think
ULTRIX will recognize a drive that doesn't a device entry.  It could
also be the Optical/Direct Access problem.

