SOMF wrote:
> 
> Any hints on disabling the on board video in a Starion 910, I recently
> purchased a Diamond card but every time I reboot Win 95 tries to
> install the onboard video. Any help will be greatly apreciated....

The BIOS auto disables the on-board S3 when during boot it detects a new
video controller. Once Win95 boots up, Win95 still sees the on-board,
but if you check carefully, you'll notice that the device is disabled.
Check in the Device Manager under the Display Adapter properties for the
S3 and you'll see that the S3 is disabled. Don't try to remove the S3
entry in the Device Manager as the next time you boot, Win95 will again
see the device. Its not really being loaded. If it was you would not see
video from the new controller.

