    We've had a small farm of 275Mhz alphas (3000/900s) for sometime
    now (see diagram copied below):
                        ___
          (alfalfa)----[ g ]---------------------------- to backbone ring
          (beans)------[ i ]
          (corn)-------[ g ]-------(scythe - fileserver)
          (oats)-------[ a ]
          (rye)--------[ s ]-------(thresher - tape-silo - coming soon)
          (wheat)------[_w_]

   and it gets quite a workout.  We use DQS for scheduling
   which supports PVM but most people just run single CPU
   jobs.  In our environment, having all of one machine is
   probably better than having 1/6 of 6 machines, anyway.

   For our next purchase, I think we are leaning towards
   an SMP machine (e.g., a 4-cpu 4100).

