The DOE ASCI system wanted a tera-flop.
You need a thousand gigaflop machines (== BIP) to get a teraflop.

The problem that Digital had in the ASCI program was a growth path to
1,000 CPU's.

The problem may not be technology. One can argue if it makes sense to
invest the money and people to design systems that can go to 1,000
CPU's. You're better off, from a market persepective, in making very
fast 1-CPU systems and scaling that to ~64 CPU's.

-- 
