Jim Matthews  <jtmatth@nswc.navy.mil> wrote:
}The TL822 DLT Automated Tape Library has three TZ88 tape drives with 
}three SCSI ports.  I've noticed in the Digital Systems & Options catalog 
}that the DEC 4100 only supports two FNSE SCSI cards (KZPAA-AA).  So my 
}questions are:

}1) How do you connect a TL822 DLT Automated Tape Library to a computer 
}system that has only two SCSI ports available?  Or re-phrased - what's 
}the proper way to setup the TL822?

}2) Wouldn't there be a performance hit if you daisy chain the TL822 SCSI 
}ports?

     We have a TL810 which has 4 TZ87's in it.  You can mess
     around with the SCSI cabling to get a variety of connections.
     We do it the "standard" way:

        +-----+        ..TL810....................
        | CPU |        :                         :
        |  SCSI--------:-[tape]--[tape]--[robot] :
        |     |        :                         :
        |  SCSI--------:-[tape]--[tape]          :
        |     |        :                         :
        +-----+        ...........................

     I don't see how 2 of these tape drives can saturate a Fast SCSI bus
     (even if both of them happened to be xfer'ing at the same time).

John
