"Dr. Vibhas Aravamuthan" <vibs@varuna.eng.lsu.edu> writes:

> 
> Hi everyone 
> Does anybody out there have any experiences regarding setting up a
> cluster of high performance alphas (433 or 500 Mhz EV5) using 
> a high speed network like HiPPi, FDDI or ATM. The other important thing
> is is there any problem about using DEC's High Performance Fortran
> compiler on such a cluster. If anybody has any positive or negative
> experiences please post or e-mail.
> Thanks in advance
--

We have a cluster of ~32 300-Mhz 21164-based systems, each with 256MB
of memory.

For the current network, we used 100-BaseT ethernets, and Bay 28115
fast ethernet switches. These can deliver ~10MByte/sec and are very
cheap.  We're now beginning to add more nodes using Myrinet. This can
do ~40 MByte/sec using TCP/IP, and ~60 MB/sec using native myrinet
API.

I haven't used the DEC HPF Fortran on that cluster. Our scientific
users mainly use PVM and MPI.

-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



