I would expect the difference to be in "expandability". Digital has
a long tradition for that "expandability" (faster busses, more busses,
more disks, more memory) is relative expensive compared to MHz. So you
may get a very fast and cheap processor, but it could f.ex. be max.
2 IDE disks and 128 MB memory (NOTE: I do not know anything - I am just
trying
to explain how it *could* be). Compare f.ex. the price of a highend
Alpha-workstation with the price of a 1 CPU Alpha 8n00. The processor
is about the same, but there is a price difference as big as a mountain,
because the 8n00 can be expanded to a mega-monster.

