This is not a hardware question, this is a software question. Ask 
yourself what operating system, development enviroment, and applications 
best fit your task, then buy the appropriate hardware.

If your local tach support only knows sparcs and pentiums, then buying a
DEC is stupid, unless you really beleive you are capable of doing all the
support yourself. Even then is it really worth your time? 

From a price/performance point of view the Alpha clones and the Pentium 
Pros are very close.



