   Bob Lombard <blombard@deltanet.com> wrote:
:Subject line about sums it up.  I've got a project hosted on a very
:creaky 11/750.  The system also has 4 RA81's and a TU80.  The OS is 
:BSD4.2 (From DEC, a loonng time ago). The 750 is falling over regularly.
:
:I have available a MVII recently pulled from service, which has the
:right controller for the 81's.  Is it too much to hope for that I can 
:simply move the RA81's to the MVII and have the whole mess boot ??
:
:Any suggestions besides the obvious of getting the 750 fixed... ?

	I don't believe that 4.2bsd proper came with MVAX II support, thus
a simple switchover won't work. However, MVAX II support was made available
I think in 4.3BSD, which is very similar, and in, of course, Ultrix, which
is also filesystem compatible. Therefore you could either:
	1)  Bring up 4.3BSD or Ultrix on the MVAX II, and then bring over
the other non-system filesystems without modification,
	2) Try to retrofit the MVAX II from 4.3BSD into 4.2BSD.

	I believe that the 4.3BSD release was considered an in situ
upgradeable from 4.2BSD. That is, it could be put place of an existing 4.2BSD
system.
	I don't know what your situation is, but I would probably strongly
consider getting another small disk, like an RD54 (I might even have one
for you cheap), put Ultrix or 4.3BSD on that, then hook up the other disks.

	Finally, I have a 750 that I could sell you spare parts from cheap.

	I also have 4.3BSD running on both the 750 and MVAXII.

