Bob Manners wrote:
> |   What always struck me as amazing, was the fact that in plain old DOS,
> |   you had pipes and globbing, and all them snazzy features of real
> |   shells. 

What few people know is that ALL-IN-1 on VMS implemented pipes a long
time ago.

One can do for instance  
 COPY ">FOR CAB$ with .FOLDER EQS ""WASTEBASKET"" DO MERGE_LINE
<.folder:30><.title:30><.created>" "sys$login:temp.txt"

The output from the command FOR CAB$.etc would be used as input for the
COPY command and be sent to the output file (temp.txt). This has some
might powerful features coupled with the scripting functions and
especially the ability to translate symbols prior to command execution,
allowing very dynamic commands !



