It seems to me you may have an tuning issue with the Prioris HX.  I
can tell you with certainty that the DEFPA adapter is capable of
better numbers than you're seeing.  Check out the following URL:

	http://www.cup.hp.com/netperf/NetperfPage.html

This is the Netperf homepage, a networking benchmark utility developed
by HP.  There's also a database of test results there that will show
you just how well the DEFPA can perform. In fact, one tester had a
system setup that was seeing performance of almost 12.5MB/s using the
DEFPA's default transmit and receive buffer settings.

Unfortunately, I have no suggestions on tuning your system, but  I
would focus on the other parts of your setup and not the DEFPA.


