Andy Leslie wrote:
> VMS revenues have always supported the corporation and subsidised all kinds
> of madness in the 1980's.
> 
> If DIGITAL sold VMS, it would presage the wholesale slaughter of many fine
> products and the breakup of the company into many parts 

The breakup began very quickly after Mr Palmer took over. Remember DEC
sold its disk drive business, sold off many software packages, killed of
many others, sold off it venerable terminal business. Recently, Dec spun
off Alta Vista software into a separate company with Alta Vista shares
traded separately from DEC's.

While it was true that VMS was the cash cow for Digital and allowed the
later to thinker with new toys such as Alpha etc, Digital has stated
many times that its growth area will be UNIX and NT (especially NT). It
is a question of time before VMS looses its cash cow status. And as soon
as Digital can survive without VMS, it may sell it off and use the
proceeds to shore up those divisions which Digital thinks have long term
future.



